              "message": "ci: run the test and web jobs through the shared gate (#1112)\n\n* ci: run the test and web jobs through the shared gate\n\nci.yml ran its own test (Linux, Windows) and wasm jobs. Both now call craft-common-actions'\ngate.yml, as the CI workflow rules ask (storytold/craft-common-actions#118):\n- test: `cargo xtask ci` on Linux (fmt, clippy, tests, wasm check); clippy and tests on Windows.\n- web: clippy for wasm32 and packaging/web/package.sh with trunk 0.21.14, in its own cache.\nThe gate saves caches from main only, so pull requests stop writing their own.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: the test gate installs no cargo tools\n\nNothing in it runs nextest, and installing it fell back to cargo-binstall on both legs.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* ci: call the shared gate at main\n\nstorytold/craft-common-actions#119 is merged, so main's gate takes an empty packages list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: FredApps <FredApps@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
